%N A163879 Number of nXnXn triangular binary arrays with all 1s connected, and a path of 1s from peak vertex to anywhere on the bottom side.
%C A163879 Can be computed using a(n) = D(n,0) - D(n,1) - D(n-1,0) + D(n-1,1), where D(n,k) is the number of connected (non-null) induced subgraphs in the triangular grid graph with n vertices on each each side and k of the 3 corner vertices removed. - _Andrew Howroyd_, Aug 31 2026
